<title>USA: Lancaster Colony CEO Gerlach dies.</title>
<headline>Lancaster Colony CEO Gerlach dies.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ohio 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lancaster Colony Corp said that John B. &quot;Bernie&quot; Gerlach, its chairman and chief executive, died on Friday after a recent illness.</p>
<p>Gerlach, 70, founded Lancaster in 1961 with his father, and directed its growth as a manufacturer and marketer of glassware, candles and other products. Its current annual sales are over $800 million.</p>
</text>
